# Deeply nested match expressions must not exhaust the Rust stack.
# Previously, each level of match used block_on_anywhere() in the MatchDispatch
# continuation, which caused recursive async context nesting and stack overflow
# for depths > ~50. The iterative fix (.await in apply_cont) keeps all
# async state on the heap, allowing arbitrary nesting depth.
#
# This test builds 100 levels of nested match by chaining through a recursive
# function — each call dispatches a match and recurses into the arm body.
[
    depth-match: [fn [let n]
        [match n
            0:   "done"
            ...: [depth-match [- n 1]]]]

    result: [depth-match 100]
]

---

%.result
=== out
String("done")
